# "This land enters tapped unless you control a Swamp or a Mountain" (CR 614.1c): Bot1 controls only a Plains on turn 3,
# so the Encampment enters tapped and cannot tap for {W} (the refusal). The positive control for the Mountain is the
# scenario where it enters beside one and activates the same turn; the control for the Swamp type is
# dalkovan-encampment-enters-untapped-beside-a-swamp-by-type.

# Only lands Bot1 controls count: Bot2's Mountain does not (the control is dalkovan-encampment-enters-untapped-beside-a-swamp-by-type
# and the Mountain in the scenario of its ability). Tapped, it cannot tap for {W} and its {2}{W}, {T} ability is refused even
# with three Moxen to pay the rest (the refusals).

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Dalkovan Encampment
Plains x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Plains x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Dalkovan Encampment.Play
! Bot1.Battlefield.Dalkovan Encampment.Activate(Ability: {T}: Add {W})
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
! Bot1.Battlefield.Dalkovan Encampment.Activate(Ability: Whenever you attack)
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Dalkovan Encampment.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield = Mountain
